W-13 review round 1: Request changes. Fix the Must fix items below, rerun checks (e2e in a copy again, plus lint/typecheck/test/format), then report again in the same format. Don't commit.

Must fix
1. No axe or title check on `/auth/callback` (Verifying) in any spec. 08:70 lists "both callbacks", so the AC "zero axe violations per screen" fails. The reviewer showed it can be checked: hold `/v1/me` with page.route while on the callback, call flow.checkScreen(), then release. That passed with 0 violations and the title "Confirming your identity · Nordlight". Put it in `chooseAndVerify` (fixtures.ts:88-100):
```ts
let release!: () => void; const held = new Promise<void>(r => (release = r));
await page.route('**/v1/me', async r => { if (page.url().includes('/auth/callback')) await held; await r.continue(); });
// click Confirm → waitForURL('**/auth/callback**') → flow.checkScreen() → release()
```
   Also: happy and declined never check the PaymentReturn Polling screen (only payment-slow does). Add that check too. To keep it stable, first fix the checkScreen race: fixtures.ts:45-49 resumes the clock during analyze() and reads the title afterwards. The reviewer reproduced it on Polling in payment_declined: the order failed during axe and the app redirected to Review. Read the title and h1 before resume(). After pauseAt, assert the URL and h1 are unchanged. Add a short comment that pauseAt(now+1s) moves app time forward.
2. payment-declined.spec.ts:27-29: the 09 row requires "second pay page with a new orderId". Record page.url() after the first payFromReview, then assert the second pay URL differs (they hold different ord_ ids).

